# ns2MJB

Nintendo Switch 2 Minecraft Jailbreak Research Project

## Overview

ns2MJB is an experimental Nintendo Switch 2 security research project exploring the possibility of using Minecraft Bedrock Edition's JavaScript scripting environment as an entry point for homebrew development and security research.

The project focuses on investigating Minecraft's scripting capabilities, runtime behavior, security restrictions, and potential vulnerabilities.

Currently, no working jailbreak or system-level exploit has been confirmed.

## Development

ns2MJB is currently under active development. The project involves researching JavaScript execution within Minecraft Bedrock, testing scripting limitations, and investigating potential security vulnerabilities.

Testing on real Nintendo Switch 2 hardware is planned, but compatibility and functionality have not yet been verified.

## Release Information

There is currently no confirmed release date for ns2MJB.

The project may not be publicly released for several weeks or longer, depending on development progress, testing, and technical limitations.

A release is not guaranteed, and additional time may be required to verify functionality and address potential issues.

Updates will be provided as development progresses.

## Disclaimer

ns2MJB is an independent research project and is not affiliated with Nintendo, Mojang, or Microsoft.

This project is experimental and should not currently be considered a functional Nintendo Switch 2 jailbreak.
